                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "987ed52f-0399-4752-870a-1f8f8bd2b5f5",
                        "source_entry_id": "04545cad-f6b6-33c1-9360-c74957bef7f2",
                        "source_sense_id": "0f462e7f-9822-3d80-922b-bebbd1378ec0",
                        "target_lang_word": "inlay",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "inlay",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e4986cb3-c247-30bc-b51c-5640d7c685c0",
                                        "entry_id": "5b545875-baf1-37ef-a0c8-1cf5bc58ac39",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To place (pieces of a foreign material) within another material to form a decorative design."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "also",
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "310de0a5-2bf5-432e-9f02-766305fb2d87",
                                                "sense_id": "e4986cb3-c247-30bc-b51c-5640d7c685c0",
                                                "text": "The body of the Scriptures hath in it limbs taken from other bodies; and in the vvord of God, are the vvords of other men, other authors, inlaid & inſerted. But, this vvork is onely vvhere the Holy Ghoſt is the VVorkman: It is not for man to inſert, to inlay other vvords into the vvord of God."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b28e5099-5f42-37ce-ac97-65094d0847a3",
                                        "entry_id": "5b545875-baf1-37ef-a0c8-1cf5bc58ac39",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To place an inlay in a tooth."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f8398b9c-b471-42b6-a11c-bb9459709517",
                                                "sense_id": "b28e5099-5f42-37ce-ac97-65094d0847a3",
                                                "text": "Porcelain inlaying is a grand thing in certain cases, and it is much to be regretted that the present existing circumstances do not warrant its being used more extensively."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4c77947b-00e5-4fcc-bd6c-4357b9966968",
                                                "sense_id": "b28e5099-5f42-37ce-ac97-65094d0847a3",
                                                "text": "It is not strange that this principle of inlaying should occur to those men years ago, for it was one of the most ancient of arts and it had been brought well-nigh to perfection. The thought of restoring broken surface in teeth, as was being done in gold and wood was ever present with them."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d6339d68-6f97-4386-831f-0590fc8ff8c9",
                                                "sense_id": "b28e5099-5f42-37ce-ac97-65094d0847a3",
                                                "text": "It is hard to tell whether it was the solid block inlay idea of itself, or else something to help cement to be retained in a cavity, that has brought about inlaying of cavities;"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "82ba2370-08ec-4b66-b22f-e3b5a5b2245b",
                                                "sense_id": "b28e5099-5f42-37ce-ac97-65094d0847a3",
                                                "text": "They felt with a prophetic instinct that sometime and somewhere these obstacles would be removed, that difficulties apparently unsurmountable would be overcome, and that the principle of inlaying teeth would become recognized as good practice in restoring broken-down tooth tissues."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "inlay",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cf3166e1-7814-3296-844b-e9fd0e912856",
                                        "entry_id": "19f5383f-04b6-3313-8e51-abf06875d8d6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The material placed within a different material in the form of a decoration."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5dcb935d-df4b-3146-ad81-539e4816a367",
                                        "entry_id": "19f5383f-04b6-3313-8e51-abf06875d8d6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A filling for a tooth, made of ceramic or gold to fit the cavity and shape of tooth and cemented into place."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f677b852-48d4-3a5c-9788-fcef8501782f",
                                        "entry_id": "19f5383f-04b6-3313-8e51-abf06875d8d6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The piece of paper or the booklet inside the case of a compact disc, DVD, or cassette."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ff966297-2f74-4a5e-83cf-be4c93a8f2ca",
                                                "sense_id": "f677b852-48d4-3a5c-9788-fcef8501782f",
                                                "text": "Putting it all together: the cassette’s been run through a labelling machine, and now this Heath Robinsonesque device adds the inlay and the box in one swift operation, taking about three seconds for each cassette."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
